cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, plus the ETCCDI references in inst/CITATION."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
title: "climatekit: Unified Climate Indices for Temperature, Precipitation, and Drought"
abstract: >
  Compute the standard suite of climate indices from daily weather
  observations: temperature (frost / ice / summer days, tropical
  nights, growing-season length, diurnal range, ETCCDI extreme-value
  indices, calendar-day percentile indices, warm and cold spell
  duration), precipitation (PRCPTOT, RX1day, RX5day, SDII, R10mm,
  R20mm, Rnnmm, CDD, CWD, R95p, R99p), drought (SPI, SPEI, PET),
  agroclimatic (Huglin, Winkler, Branas, frost dates), and comfort
  (wind chill, heat index, humidex, fire danger). Pure R, no API
  calls, tidy data-frame outputs.
authors:
